prompt:
Use case: ads-marketing.
Asset type: ONE finished Chrome Web Store promotional tile, exactly 11:7 landscape rectangle, approximately 1760x1120, intended for 440x280.
Primary request: a confident, clean English promo for YouTube Live Chat Fullscreen that IMMEDIATELY looks like YouTube's actual native live chat.
Input image role: STYLE REFERENCE ONLY for the live-chat UI anatomy. Do not copy the reference's game, streamer, usernames, messages, specific avatars, or branding. Create all-new original scene and fictional chat.
Composition: a modern editorial food-livestream visual, one normal widescreen video filling most of the lower part of the tile. Warm daylight scene of anonymous adult chef's hands making a beautiful ramen bowl in a bright kitchen, no faces, no restaurant logos. App-like, warm, inviting, real entertainment. The top band is near-black #0f0f0f with LARGE beautiful white sans-serif headline on two compact lines EXACTLY "Fullscreen" and "Live Chat". A thin restrained red line provides accent. Type must be legible at 220x140 and fit wholly inside safe margins. Fullscreen MUST be one unbroken word (F-u-l-l-s-c-r-e-e-n), never Full Screen; Live Chat has a space.
Inside the right 31% of this SAME video, one dark YouTube-native chat overlay. Flat matte near-black rectangular panel, modest 3px-radius look, not a floating glossy card.
Native header exactly "Top chat" with a small downward chevron beside it and small vertical three dots at far right; thin understated separator.
The chat body MUST be a real-looking compact conversation list, not generic abstract horizontal lines, not rounded speech bubbles, not separate message cards. Around 7 short rows. Each row has a small circular varied profile avatar on the left; muted-gray handle followed immediately by a white message ON THE SAME BASELINE. Example fictional rows EXACTLY:
@alex  that looks so good
@mira  hello chat!
@sam  chef mode 🔥
@nova  recipe please
@lee  let's go
@jules  perfect timing
@river  hungry now 😄
Use natural proportional YouTube-like sans-serif text, small but clearly actual letters, compact line-height with sensible breathing room. Some names bold gray, one name subtle green, ordinary messages white. No giant avatars or rows. Avatars are small original abstract/profile icons, no real people.
Native footer: a small self-avatar and plain text placeholder "Chat..." above a subtle underline, a small smiley outline and small outlined send triangle on the right. No giant pill input box or filled Telegram-looking button. These UI controls stay inside the same panel. All this must look recognizably like the exact reference YouTube live-chat anatomy.
Keep food clearly visible left of panel. Native panel fits inside video and does not dominate more than a third. No physical screen hardware, no browser tabs, no room/desk setup, no gamer neon or cars, no 3D glossy glass panels. No YouTube/Chrome official logo, fake store status or creator endorsement, extra slogans, watermark, or screenshot claims. This is original illustrative promotional art with fictional chat. One finished artwork, not a grid or a contact sheet.
